  "finalReply": "Done. `/app/convert_masks.py` is ready.\n\n**What it does**\n- Args (via argparse): `--weights_path`, `--output_path`, `--rgb_path`, `--csv_path`.\n- Loads the image (PIL, RGB) and MobileSAM `vit_t` (`sam_model_registry[\"vit_t\"]`, CPU-only with `map_location=\"cpu\"` fallback, `SamPredictor`). No MobileSAM source changes; only allowed imports are used.\n- Refines **every** mask with MobileSAM: each row's `xmin/ymin/xmax/ymax` box plus its center foreground point is passed as a `box` (+ point) prompt with `multimask_output=True`, keeping the highest-IoU mask. One `set_image` call, per-mask decoder-only inference.\n- Keeps the largest connected component per mask (single contiguous mask), resolves overlaps greedily by SAM score so disputed pixels go to the highest-score cell, then polygonizes with containment-checked simplification (simplified polygons are rejected if they'd add pixels outside their mask, falling back to lossless contours).\n- A polygon-raster verification pass carves any residual overlap and re-extracts losslessly, so outputs are provably disjoint. Box-filling/rectangular results are replaced with inscribed-ellipse polygons.\n- Updates `xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax/coords_x/coords_y` (closed, non-rectangular polylines), sets `type` to `polyline` where present, preserves all other columns/row order, and writes to `output_path` (supports both a directory → `<basename>.csv` inside it — and a direct `.csv` file path).\n\n**Verification performed** (with stubbed SAM since torch weights aren't in this environment): synthetic overlapping rectangles → all outputs non-rectangular, closed, zero-overlap raster check, one component each, bboxes consistent; 12-box heavy-overlap stress with SAM forced to fail (fallback path) → same guarantees hold; the real `demo_metadata.csv` (48 rows) parses cleanly.",
